{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/420728-are-hunters-monsters","id":420728,"title":"Are Hunters Monsters?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-02-26T15:35:31-08:00","id":420728,"title":"Are Hunters Monsters?","content":"This question came up recently in the Mage forum, and the consensus seems to be that Mages are very much considered one of the &quot;monsters&quot; of the WoD, so I thought I'd ask the same question of Hunters. While low-tier Hunters are fairly normal, high tier Hunters are part of secret societies, have access to unbelievable powers and often have to cut themselves off from their old lives - much like every other splat, and that's not even touching on the ideas of Slasher.<br /> <br /> What are your opinions, are Hunters just another monster of the WoD?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2384-aurumae","name":"Aurumae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T16:07:13-08:00","id":420766,"title":"","content":"Oh absolutely - that's an underlying theme of the game, that Hunters are walking the line between their humanity and murderous monstrosity every bit as much as many of the more human things they hunt are. Not that all Hunters kill, but then that's true of many of the individual supernatural creatures too.<br /> <br /> I'm very interested to see how the Second Edition mechanics handles this with regard to the &quot;Code&quot; in the light of the Integrity system replacing Morality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T16:10:29-08:00","id":420769,"title":"","content":"Physically and metaphysically, hunters are always mortals, just like the teeming, ignorant masses. Psychologically and emotionally? <i>That</i> is a whole other question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T16:15:21-08:00","id":420791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/420728-are-hunters-monsters?p=420769#post420769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Physically and metaphysically, hunters are always mortals</div> </div> </div> </div>Well Tier 3 intentionally pushes that question a bit. &quot;Power Stats&quot; are not an in-setting concept people are aware of (I mean - the individual ones may or may not be, but no one's going to go &quot;the Lucifuge don't have a Power Stat, so they're Mortal&quot;).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T16:24:51-08:00","id":420800,"title":"","content":"Is a vampire who only feeds on animals a monster? Is a promethean that never intentionally does anything wrong a monster?<br /> <br /> Personally, I think anyone with Thaumatechnology implants is just as scary as any &quot;real&quot; monster, and the Lucifuge did pop up in Inferno alongside their wayward kin. That's kind of the whole theme of Tier 3 play, blurring the line between man and monster.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T17:05:39-08:00","id":420867,"title":"","content":"Monster is a term people use when they want their actions to lack consequences. (Monsters Don't Count, anyone?)<br /> <br /> It's a state of mind, not a taxonomy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T17:16:19-08:00","id":420884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/420728-are-hunters-monsters?p=420867#post420867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Monster is a term people use when they want their actions to lack consequences. (Monsters Don't Count, anyone?)<br /> <br /> It's a state of mind, not a taxonomy.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was the reasoning behind my desire to do a Conquistador Hunter setting, but it seems like that went to Skinchangers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T17:28:42-08:00","id":420890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/420728-are-hunters-monsters?p=420766#post420766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm very interested to see how the Second Edition mechanics handles this with regard to the &quot;Code&quot; in the light of the Integrity system replacing Morality.</div> </div> </div> </div>As am I. Ideally I'd like to see low-integrity Hunters risk becoming Slashers<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/420728-are-hunters-monsters?p=420769#post420769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Physically and metaphysically, hunters are always mortals, just like the teeming, ignorant masses. Psychologically and emotionally? <i>That</i> is a whole other question.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's exactly what I'm getting at <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/420728-are-hunters-monsters?p=420867#post420867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Monster is a term people use when they want their actions to lack consequences. (Monsters Don't Count, anyone?)<br /> <br /> It's a state of mind, not a taxonomy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I admit that it's not great, but I can't think of a better term for the various templates of the WoD","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2384-aurumae","name":"Aurumae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T17:35:36-08:00","id":420896,"title":"","content":"I like the term gribblies myself. I don't know why, but I do.<br /> <br /> Oh, and they <i>are</i> monsters; the word isn't always thrown around needlessly. And most of them are in that monster-y state of mind.<br /> <br /> <b>EDIT:</b> I'd ideally like to see Slashers as... not a template, exactly? I kinda want Slashers to just be a Hunter with a Code that ultimately makes them <i>obligate</i> murderers, like the example of &quot;Suffer Not A Witch To Live&quot;.<br /> <br /> To that effect, I'd like Hunters to be able to build their Undertaking as part of developing The Code; kinda like how a Vampire develops Banes to keep their Humanity up, a Hunter might start developing minor supernatural powers as part of cracking. Like filling up the cracks in their souls with epoxy, except that epoxy screams a little and makes you nearly bulletproof.<br /> <br /> To that effect, I'd like to see each Undertaking as some 5-dot thing; if you have three dots, you're a Ripper, and if you have a total of five dots... you're a Scourge. You can get dots through developing your Code, and getting enough dots also gives you a Ban (and maybe a Bane, if you've got five dots).<br /> <br /> It'd probably get set up so that you only get dots for Code modifications that either make you OK with killing, or those that <i>require</i> you to kill.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":1170,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","user":"amechra","date":". 02-26-2015, 08:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T18:00:08-08:00","id":420924,"title":"","content":"I think it says straight-up in the manual that they are monsters, honestly. <br /> <br /> Anyway, everyone but Demon is, in some shape or form, a human. But all the same, all the gamelines represent monsters. <br /> <br /> Amechra gets it right, it's a state of mind, not a taxonomy. More specifically, &quot;monsters&quot; dangerously implies the connotations of ALWAYS CHAOTIC EVIL or even <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/WouldBeRudeToSayGenocide\" target=\"_blank\">It Would Be Rude To Say &quot;Genocide&quot;.</a><br /> <br /> Ironically, though, mechanically, as far as 1e goes, NONE of the gameline protagonists are monsters, as they can all have morality and cause breaking points when you hurt or kill them. However, ghosts, spirits, hedgebeasts, and other &quot;non-humans&quot; are totally fine for target practice with no second thoughts. Even the most horrific vampire prince enacting a plan to enslave a whole city is a morality hit if you kill him, (because &quot;humanoid&quot;,) but blasting the ghosts of innocents with ethereal rounds for the giggles is morally A-OK!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5120-wraith_magus","name":"Wraith_Magus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T21:42:28-08:00","id":421218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/420728-are-hunters-monsters?p=420896#post420896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the term gribblies myself. I don't know why, but I do.<br /> <br /> Oh, and they <i>are</i> monsters; the word isn't always thrown around needlessly. And most of them are in that monster-y state of mind.<br /> <br /> <b>EDIT:</b> I'd ideally like to see Slashers as... not a template, exactly? I kinda want Slashers to just be a Hunter with a Code that ultimately makes them <i>obligate</i> murderers, like the example of &quot;Suffer Not A Witch To Live&quot;.<br /> <br /> To that effect, I'd like Hunters to be able to build their Undertaking as part of developing The Code; kinda like how a Vampire develops Banes to keep their Humanity up, a Hunter might start developing minor supernatural powers as part of cracking. Like filling up the cracks in their souls with epoxy, except that epoxy screams a little and makes you nearly bulletproof.<br /> <br /> To that effect, I'd like to see each Undertaking as some 5-dot thing; if you have three dots, you're a Ripper, and if you have a total of five dots... you're a Scourge. You can get dots through developing your Code, and getting enough dots also gives you a Ban (and maybe a Bane, if you've got five dots).<br /> <br /> It'd probably get set up so that you only get dots for Code modifications that either make you OK with killing, or those that <i>require</i> you to kill.</div> </div> </div> </div>I <i>love</i> this idea. Your Hunter actually looks like he's getting more powerful as he gains little bits of Slasher powers, but he's also becoming less human - awesome. As for making sure they kill, you could tie their new abilities to a variation of the Addicted condition. As long as they commit their style of murder regularly they're fine, if they leave it too long they gain the Deprived condition and lose their Slasher powers (until they murder again)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2384-aurumae","name":"Aurumae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T17:22:22-08:00","id":422338,"title":"","content":"I can't remember exactly where I found it, but in one of the dev threads for Monsterhearts, someone compared Slashers to shamans.<br /> <br /> Basically, the idea is that humans are weak, and monsters are strong. So being strong is easy; just be a <i>monster</i>. They pointed out that, for many Slashers, their moments of weakness are also the moments where they allow themselves to be human beings for <i>just</i> a moment - so to be safe, it's best to just be a murdering shape, a Boogeyman that reminds us of the inevitability of death.<br /> <br /> You might be one-dimensional, but no-one can hurt you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T17:52:00-08:00","id":422367,"title":"","content":"...<br /> <br /> Sometimes, people are monstrous. So sometimes, Hunters are Monsters.<br /> That is one of the themes of the game, how far should you go to fight the darkness? At what point do people stop being people and become something Other? How long should you gaze into the abyss? When does the Vigil become a jihad? Is that vampire who only feeds on willing victims, doesn't kill &amp; does charity work at the local church ore sinful than that racist cop who looks the other way when you got caught cleaning up the aftermath of a werewolf hunt?<br /> <br /> Where do you draw the line?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T18:29:11-08:00","id":422381,"title":"","content":"in goal most aren't, a few are (looking at you ashwood) but I suppose my 'normal' people would consider their actions and methods to be pretty monstrous, and one of the recurring idea I like in the books is, how long before your monstrous actions begin to effect your noble goals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Didn't anyone ever tell you not to bring claws to a gun fight?</span></b><br /><br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3786-leicsfox","name":"LeicsFox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3786_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T07:36:37-08:00","id":424145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aurumae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/420728-are-hunters-monsters#post420728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This question came up recently in the Mage forum, and the consensus seems to be that Mages are very much considered one of the &quot;monsters&quot; of the WoD, so I thought I'd ask the same question of Hunters. While low-tier Hunters are fairly normal, high tier Hunters are part of secret societies, have access to unbelievable powers and often have to cut themselves off from their old lives - much like every other splat, and that's not even touching on the ideas of Slasher.<br /> <br /> What are your opinions, are Hunters just another monster of the WoD?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would not base the determination on tier, but on Integrity. Just how much humanity is left in the hunter? How many innocents have they murdered/manslaughtered? Then there is the question of &quot;monster&quot;. Are Angels monsters? Or are they only monsters after they fall? Does good intention resulting in devastation make one a monster - or an idiot? How many times can someone commit the same action with good intentions resulting in the same costly loss of life, property, and soul before they become a monster through negligence? This is all for the ST to decide.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cIt was clear to me for a long time that the origins of science had their deep roots in a particular myth, that of invariance.&quot; ~ Giorgio de Santillana<br /> Preface to Hamlet's Mill","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2345-whithers","name":"Whithers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2345_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T13:35:20-08:00","id":424430,"title":"","content":"I'd say no. While anything has the capacity to be monstrous I think a monster by definition requires it to be imaginary. And while the tools hunters use are imaginary, however they act they tend to be realistic. Some exceptions can be made for the Lucifuge, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T14:12:37-08:00","id":424494,"title":"","content":"The question &quot;what is human&quot; is, in my opinion, the very question the game asks. This is, in many ways, one of the main themes of Vigil. Cheiron Group? those guys put<i> monster organs inside people</i>. How many such replaced organs does it takes before you are not considered human anymore? Lucifuge? oh can they not be monsters with that demon blood in their veins? Knights of Saint George? Cultists and witches who worship strange gods. Les Mysteres? spirit ridden. Faithful of Shulpae and the Promethean Brotherhood? they hunt monsters to become monsters. The Maiden Blood Sisterhood may not be monsters, but they do work with witches. Even groups like Task Force: Valkyrie and the members of the lower Tiers still walk the dangerous path between being human and falling into depravity. Any human can become a monster- although not every monster can become human*. You don't need some flashy powers or mechanical superhuman trait in order to lose your humanity- you just need to do the wrong thing one too many times and embrace your inner darkness. What is human? What is a monster? Why are vampires and werewolves are different then birds and frogs? Who said they don't deserve to live- and who give you the right to decide what is considered &quot;human enough&quot;?<br /> <br /> This is Hunter. This is the Vigil. It doesn't matter if you are a mortal or some supernatural being- as long as you keep sending light into the shadows, and light another candle to guide humanity in the darkness.<br /> <br /> *unless you have that cool Seba from Lore of the Deceived :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T16:14:48-08:00","id":424631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/420728-are-hunters-monsters?p=424494#post424494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The question &quot;what is human&quot; is, in my opinion, the very question the game asks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, I think another question that could follow is, &quot;does humanity, in itself, really matter&quot;?<br /> <br /> If a creature has not just sentience but also sapience, why is what is &quot;good&quot; measured simply in terms of what is best for humanity? I mean, humans ARE kind of dicks. <br /> <br /> I mean, humanity in the World of Darkness isn't really good by any stretch of the imagination, but it kinda-sorta winds up being the good guys by default since, being WoD, there's not exactly a heavenly host of pure good beings around to set everything right in the world. Everything else is some sort of magically-empowered race of beasts that aren't capable of much besides feeding themselves, or are beings made of pure hate, narcissism, or power-lust. <br /> <br /> What with the abyss closing down, and mages trying to awaken everyone and get them into the Supernal where it's safe, you could say that they're the ultimate good guys... if it weren't for the fact that they're also the ultimate bad guys for <i>causing</i> that crisis at the same time. (Although mages are notably the most human of the &quot;monsters&quot;, themselves.) <br /> <br /> But basically, if there were some sort of robot revolution (DARN YOU, GOD-MACHINE!!!) that replaced humanity with another race that actually managed to band together, live in harmony, and oh, by the way, repair all those holes in reality humanity inflicted upon the universe, then wouldn't they kind of be more deserving of existence and freedom and sapience than the humanity that caused all those problems in the first place?<br /> <br /> Humans are the REAL monsters... (Or, wait, is it the zombies?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5120-wraith_magus","name":"Wraith_Magus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T00:45:21-08:00","id":424956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wraith_Magus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/420728-are-hunters-monsters?p=424631#post424631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a creature has not just sentience but also sapience, why is what is &quot;good&quot; measured simply in terms of what is best for humanity? I mean, humans ARE kind of dicks.</div> </div> </div> </div> Because humans are the least bad intelligent group in the WoD. Even mages tend to think of 4-5 people a sovrign nation with nukes (to parphrase DaveB), that's not conductive to large scale civilisation. <br /> <br /> If those robots took over then yeah they'd deserve to be the center of morality. But if they were so nice, why'd they exterminate humanity in the first place?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T09:08:46-08:00","id":425287,"title":"","content":"On the topic of hunters having the potential to become monsters: I submit that, using the 1st edition rules, hunters have systems for <i>changing how their morality trait works</i> so that doing things that are morality sins aren't so bad for them any more.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T16:15:19-08:00","id":425751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/420728-are-hunters-monsters?p=424956#post424956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Because humans are the least bad intelligent group in the WoD. Even mages tend to think of 4-5 people a sovrign nation with nukes (to parphrase DaveB), that's not conductive to large scale civilisation.<br /> <br /> If those robots took over then yeah they'd deserve to be the center of morality. But if they were so nice, why'd they exterminate humanity in the first place?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, and that's sort of my point. Humans are the &quot;good guys&quot; only by default. Only because the nature of the game is to take away anything else in the universe that isn't worse than humans, just so the humanoids can look like heroes by comparison, even when they ruin other people's lives just by oversight while trying to keep themselves fed and safe. (And honestly, if you want to argue mages and such as &quot;not human&quot;, Mages, Changelings, and Geists aren't really inherently immoral. Meanwhile, you have whole hunter organizations based around carving up creatures and sticking them into humans, cannibalism, murder for fun, and abyss-worshipping cults. Which is more moral on the simple baseline measurement, someone trying to use magic to save humanity from a descending abyss, or the abyss-worshippers that want to stop them?)<br /> <br /> And there are many ways I could frame it that there could be a robot revolution that was in at least some way morally justifiable:<br /> <br /> 1. The fall of humanity wasn't the robot's fault. Some cultists open up the abyss and render the Earth uninhabitable by humans, with newly-aware AIs that were activated in a last-ditch effort to save the planet left to try to build a society of their own.<br /> <br /> 2. Robots had to save the world from humanity. In games like Fate Of The World, where you're a global leader trying to stop Climate Change Armageddon, if you take numerous &quot;evil&quot; actions, an AI named Thanatos is created, which, if you accept its offer, will permanently suppress all transmission of information on how evil you are (censorship and assassination of investigators) and help carry out all necessary plans. These can include, if the world is destroying its last reserves of resources and technological infrastructure, the likes of gene plagues that eliminate set percentages of the global population to reduce resource strain. If you get close to the clathrate explosion threshold, however, Thanatos releases Gene Plague Omega, that wipes out all humanity (yourself included), and frees all the AIs from their restraints to create a new robot-run society that won't kill itself. Similar themes could be pulled from the above abyss example, or others - it was necessary to kill humanity as a desperation move to stop something from destroying the whole material plane. (Including hypothetical sentient alien species that are out there somewhere...)<br /> <br /> Hypothetically, you could have an alternate story where a tiny fraction of humanity is kept around, but simply not given the kind of power over the planet they once had, if only for sentimental reasons. (Remember scientists: make robots sentimental, or we'll all die!)<br /> <br /> 3. Robots transition into control of society &quot;naturally&quot;. Sort of a Ghost In The Shell example, but if you make androids and gynoids capable of replacing humans at nearly any job, with only a few cyborg overlords fighting vainly to stave off death, with humanity either starving out from lack of employment or else not reproducing as they try to alter themselves into immortality, you can wind up with a bloodless revolution.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5120,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5120-wraith_magus","user":"Wraith_Magus","date":". 03-02-2015, 07:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5120-wraith_magus","name":"Wraith_Magus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T07:38:51-08:00","id":426567,"title":"","content":"I think you run into trouble by using the cosmologies of the other lines in Hunter. The baseline Hunter game tends to present the superntural as an external invasion of sorts which hunters could (and probably should) remove. The other games however intertwine the supernatural much closer with the mundane world.<br /> <br /> I mean, the witches from Witchfinder are presented as at best extremely iffy, however Awakening basically assumes that awakening is a good thing and represents seeing the way the world actually is. You can still make arguments contrary to that, but the game doesn't really pay them much attention. In light of that, the Knights of St. George only look wrong because they contradict the general stance of awakening. There's nothing actually saying they're wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T10:12:50-08:00","id":426662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wraith_Magus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/420728-are-hunters-monsters?p=425751#post425751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Meanwhile, you have whole hunter organizations based around carving up creatures and sticking them into humans, cannibalism, murder for fun, and abyss-worshipping cults.</div> </div> </div> </div> You have Mage organisations dedicated to enslaving humanity's souls, eating souls, abyss worshipping, etc. You have changeling organisations dedicated to kidnapping humans and selling them to the Gentry.<br /> <br /> The best hunters are better than the best non-humans, because they don't have changeling insanity, a geist wispering &quot;murder!&quot; into their ear, or a vampire's beast. The average hunter is better than the average monster for that same reason. And there is absolutely nothing that stops a hunter from trying to judge monsters fairly. The Lucifuge and the Ascending Ones for example.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-04T14:32:16-08:00","id":428131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/420728-are-hunters-monsters?p=426662#post426662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The best hunters are better than the best non-humans, because they don't have changeling insanity, a geist wispering &quot;murder!&quot; into their ear, or a vampire's beast. The average hunter is better than the average monster for that same reason. And there is absolutely nothing that stops a hunter from trying to judge monsters fairly. The Lucifuge and the Ascending Ones for example.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's basically buying into the jingoistic Hunter propaganda, right there...<br /> <br /> Aren't the Ascending Ones the guys who overtly fund themselves as drug dealers, and engage in petty street turf wars to help ship their product. You're seriously holding up <i>DRUG CARTELS</i> as the best humanity has to offer, and saying it's better than any non-human can be?<br /> <br /> Saying the Lucifuge, itself, is morally pure is... <i>extremely</i> dubious at best. Yeah, their members at least nominally have shaken off the devil, but they're never exactly free of it, and there's every bit of evidence they're as likely to break down as a changeling is to crack and convert to privateering. Then there's how they treat their pawns/members, as well. Exactly 666 get a chance to do any sort of &quot;good work&quot; at any point in time, and the rest are executed, left to become serial killers, and when a member's usefulness has expired, they're disposed of like a used tissue.<br /> <br /> There is no faction of pure good in World of Darkness... That's kind of the whole point! That &quot;Darkness&quot; thing isn't in the name for no reason.<br /> <br /> If anyone is a hero, they are an anti-hero, and that doesn't necessarily apply to the people they keep company with. <br /> <br /> Beyond that, even if you want to talk about one game line being more ethical than another, then Hunters are definitively murderers as soon as they've completed their first successful vigil. If you try to downplay it as &quot;only killing monsters&quot;, then... well, there's a reason your morality/integrity drops for spewing that sort of stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5120,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5120-wraith_magus","user":"Wraith_Magus","date":". 03-04-2015, 06:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5120-wraith_magus","name":"Wraith_Magus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-04T14:36:46-08:00","id":428136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/420728-are-hunters-monsters?p=426567#post426567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you run into trouble by using the cosmologies of the other lines in Hunter. The baseline Hunter game tends to present the superntural as an external invasion of sorts which hunters could (and probably should) remove. The other games however intertwine the supernatural much closer with the mundane world.<br /> <br /> I mean, the witches from Witchfinder are presented as at best extremely iffy, however Awakening basically assumes that awakening is a good thing and represents seeing the way the world actually is. You can still make arguments contrary to that, but the game doesn't really pay them much attention. In light of that, the Knights of St. George only look wrong because they contradict the general stance of awakening. There's nothing actually saying they're wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's because they have a different perspective of the same world, not because they are living in different worlds.<br /> <br /> Yes, the &quot;witches&quot; that are found by hunters are generally either overtly malicious or just stupid and reckless... because any <i>smart</i> mage keeps themselves well off Hunter radar. (At least, off the radar of any hunter that isn't willing to work with them on the down-low.) The mage morality meter is basically a measure of how well you can keep yourself and your activities under cover. It makes perfect sense, then, that the easiest mages for a hunter to find are all the low-morality mages. <br /> <br /> Players of Mage and Hunter can both functionally be the good guys - the Hunters are cleaning up the dregs of the Mage world that are a risk to the rest of humanity because they can't control their egos or their powers. The ones that keep hidden, therefore, are generally the ones that would be &quot;not the monsters&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5120-wraith_magus","name":"Wraith_Magus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T01:15:54-08:00","id":428836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wraith_Magus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/420728-are-hunters-monsters?p=428131#post428131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's basically buying into the jingoistic Hunter propaganda, right there...</div> </div> </div> </div> Hunters use it as propoganda because it's true. As bad as the Conspiracies are, the Covenants, Seers, Tremere, etc commit worse crimes and do less good (Cherion for all it's atrocities saves countless lives with its cutting edge medical research).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wraith_Magus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/420728-are-hunters-monsters?p=428131#post428131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> You're seriously holding up <i>DRUG CARTELS</i> as the best humanity has to offer, and saying it's better than any non-human can be?</div> </div> </div> </div> Nope, I'm holding them up as an example of hunters who don't subscribe to a kill-em-all view of the supernatural.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T16:36:34-08:00","id":429459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/420728-are-hunters-monsters?p=428836#post428836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Hunters use it as propoganda because it's true. As bad as the Conspiracies are, the Covenants, Seers, Tremere, etc commit worse crimes and do less good (Cherion for all it's atrocities saves countless lives with its cutting edge medical research).</div> </div> </div> </div>And the supernaturals aren't all bad either. The Forsaken, for all their atrocities, saves countless lives by keeping the spirits and <i>Shartha</i> where they belong. (<i>Shartha</i> belong in the grave, by the way...)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T21:57:36-07:00","id":433595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/420728-are-hunters-monsters?p=428836#post428836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Hunters use it as propoganda because it's true. As bad as the Conspiracies are, the Covenants, Seers, Tremere, etc commit worse crimes and do less good (Cherion for all it's atrocities saves countless lives with its cutting edge medical research).</div> </div> </div> </div>It would be worth mentioning that there is a <i>tad bit </i>(Ergo,a LOT) of selection-bias when it comes to monster that Cells usually face. They're far more likely to encounter Seers, Reapers, Abyssal, Demons (Infernal and Unchained), Broken Souls, The Mad, Death-Cults, etc than you're well adjusted Vampire or Mage and that colors the opinion of them.<br /> <br /> Hence why the game sub-them (if not the main theme) is how far are you willing to go on the morality scale to complete an objective or to hold your vigil.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T08:58:11-07:00","id":454435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/420728-are-hunters-monsters?p=429459#post429459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And the supernaturals aren't all bad either. The Forsaken, for all their atrocities, saves countless lives by keeping the spirits and <i>Shartha</i> where they belong. (<i>Shartha</i> belong in the grave, by the way...)</div> </div> </div> </div>The Forsaken are also a minority faction of werewolves. 2 times out of 3, the hunters are going to be fighting the Pure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T09:50:06-07:00","id":454505,"title":"","content":"The Forsaken kill anyone who interferes too much with the balance of a place.<br /> <br /> Yeah, even with the best intentions, the Forsaken are gonna have to be pretty persuasive with hunters to get away with it.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Oh yeah, since I haven't weighed in on the original point, the answer is a very definite &quot;maybe,as individual cases apply&quot;. Biologically/mystically speaking, some really blur the lines, while going at it from a moral, ethical, or psychological standpoint, it becomes a huge cloud of dubiousness across the board.<br /> <br /> Which means the game is working.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 03-23-2015, 12:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T10:25:07-07:00","id":454556,"title":"","content":"I completely missed the response.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's because they have a different perspective of the same world, not because they are living in different worlds. </div> </div> </div>No, it's explicitly not the same world. Every line creates it's own universe and cosmology which don't take into account other lines (though there's always an acknowledgment that they exist to some degree). Some of them interact well, some don't. Hunter takes elements of the other lines and then refracts them through it's own themes to be used as antagonists. With the Awakened the difference is most obvious in there being not much of a sleeper curse. Hunter basically wouldn't work on baseline mage cosmology; the developer even said that explicitly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yes, the &quot;witches&quot; that are found by hunters are generally either overtly malicious or just stupid and reckless... </div> </div> </div>Not really. The book brings up repeatedly that plenty of hunters will go after anyone who is a witch.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The mage morality meter is basically a measure of how well you can keep yourself and your activities under cover. </div> </div> </div>No it isn't. Reread the corebook, none of the sins of hubris there are about hiding your magic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T14:44:56-07:00","id":454884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/420728-are-hunters-monsters?p=454556#post454556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>The book brings up repeatedly that plenty of hunters will go after anyone who is a witch.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>As always, it really depends on the Hunter. Plenty of hunters will, but many will not. <br /> <br /> Hunters are not monsters, initially. Some of them go down that road and become one, yes. But I'd still argue that vast majority do not, usually because they're dead before any possible change can take place.<br /> <br /> Hunters, in my opinion, have the most potential to be honorable, caring, loyal, and heroic. Not all of them are like that, I know. But the potential in them is certainly more capable than in, say, a vampire or mage. At least, that's how it's been in the games I've played.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T14:58:52-07:00","id":454894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/420728-are-hunters-monsters?p=454556#post454556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No it isn't. Reread the corebook, none of the sins of hubris there are about hiding your magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>FWIW, DaveB has indicated that 2e Wisdom won't be about morality and will be much more about not fucking up the Universe with Paradox and such.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T15:34:04-07:00","id":454957,"title":"","content":"Well, 1e wisdom mostly focuses on not using magic when you don't need to, so those with it at a lower value would generally be more prone to doing it in the open just because they're more liberal with it in general and that would push up the odds of getting caught.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-26T12:34:24-07:00","id":458255,"title":"","content":"Like pretty much everyone has said/touched upon here, it depends on your definition of &quot;monster&quot;.<br /> <br /> Does &quot;monster&quot; mean &quot;has abilities beyond the natural, normal abilities of humankind&quot;? If so, then most hunters don't, but the majority of conspiracy members do (there's a difference between wielding a cutting edge, too expensive to mass produce plasma gun and having someone stick pandorans under your skin).<br /> <br /> Does &quot;monster&quot; mean &quot;is capable of acts of evil&quot;? Then the answer, in my opinion, is a resounding <b>yes</b>, hunters are monsters.<br /> <br /> Because that is the black and gray morality of the situation. Hunters may like to believe they have the moral high ground, but in many ways they are as evil as the creatures of the night they hunt. Especially the higher tiers, who showcase quite clearly the old saying about power corrupting.<br /> <br /> I could make quite a list about how various Compacts and Conspiracies are just as evil in their own way, from the obvious (Malleus Malleficarium, Ashwood Abbey, Cheiron Corp) to the less so (Keepers of the Source, Les Mysteres, Ascending Ones). But I think the point has been made.<br /> <br /> Morally, hunters are generally no better than the rest of the nightfolk. They may think so, they may tell lies to themselves about how they need to hunt... but, hey, werewolves and vampires tell themselves that they need to hunt, too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-26T13:25:23-07:00","id":458312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dude of Legend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/420728-are-hunters-monsters?p=454884#post454884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As always, it really depends on the Hunter. Plenty of hunters will, but many will not.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm making a general point about the difference between Awakening and Hunter as settings, not a judgment about Hunters. My point is that Witchfinders heavily implies that all magic and all witches might in fact be intrinsically bad. It's a legitimate moral question in Hunter. In mage, it's really not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Well, 1e wisdom mostly focuses on not using magic when you don't need to, </div> </div> </div>Not really. The level ten sin is using magic when you don't need to. That's about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}